<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
  <key>Label</key>
  <string>com.huffmanwrites.repair-plan</string>
  <key>ProgramArguments</key>
  <array>
    <string>/bin/bash</string>
    <string>/Users/prh/Developer/huffmanwrites/scripts/repair-plan-runner.sh</string>
  </array>
  <!-- Quarterly, on the first day of January, April, July and October at 07:30 CT.

       Four dictionaries, one per month, because that is the documented form:
       `man launchd.plist` types StartCalendarInterval as "dictionary of integers
       or array of dictionaries of integers", and three LaunchAgents here already
       run an array of dictionaries (docket-watch, sitrep-watchdog,
       weekly-integrity). An array of schedules is NOT LaunchDaemon-only.

       What is not supported is an array as the VALUE of a key. This file used
       Month => [1,4,7,10] inside one dictionary until 2026-11-01, on the theory
       that launchd ORs the values within a key. Measured: it fires on the 1st of
       every month. The job ran 2026-11-01 07:30, a month that is not in the list,
       and `runs = 1` in `launchctl print` confirms today was its only firing
       since the plist was installed on 2026-10-01 at 07:43. The descriptor shows
       the array faithfully, so nothing looked wrong from the outside. The
       runner now also refuses any month outside the four, which bounds the cost
       of this class of mistake to a no-op run.

       07:30 CT, thirty minutes after the ninety-days job, not 07:00 with it.
       Both land on the 1st of the month and both must finish before Philip's
       morning review, but running them in the same minute (measured
       2026-10-01: both started at 07:00:05) put two concurrent fal.ai
       submissions on the shared queue, and the two jobs' hero images came back
       crossed with each other. Sequential runs keep both clear of the Monday
       cluster (site audit 13:00, wiki check 13:30, weekly integrity 14:00)
       even when the 1st is a Monday. -->
  <key>StartCalendarInterval</key>
  <array>
    <dict>
      <key>Month</key>
      <integer>1</integer>
      <key>Day</key>
      <integer>1</integer>
      <key>Hour</key>
      <integer>7</integer>
      <key>Minute</key>
      <integer>30</integer>
    </dict>
    <dict>
      <key>Month</key>
      <integer>4</integer>
      <key>Day</key>
      <integer>1</integer>
      <key>Hour</key>
      <integer>7</integer>
      <key>Minute</key>
      <integer>30</integer>
    </dict>
    <dict>
      <key>Month</key>
      <integer>7</integer>
      <key>Day</key>
      <integer>1</integer>
      <key>Hour</key>
      <integer>7</integer>
      <key>Minute</key>
      <integer>30</integer>
    </dict>
    <dict>
      <key>Month</key>
      <integer>10</integer>
      <key>Day</key>
      <integer>1</integer>
      <key>Hour</key>
      <integer>7</integer>
      <key>Minute</key>
      <integer>30</integer>
    </dict>
  </array>
  <key>WorkingDirectory</key>
  <string>/Users/prh/Developer/huffmanwrites</string>
  <!-- Keep the exported PATH used by the other huffmanwrites jobs so hugo,
       python3, pdftotext and the keychain-backed helpers resolve the same way. -->
  <key>EnvironmentVariables</key>
  <dict>
    <key>PATH</key>
    <string>/opt/homebrew/bin:/usr/local/bin:/usr/bin:/bin:/usr/sbin:/sbin</string>
    <key>HOME</key>
    <string>/Users/prh</string>
  </dict>
  <key>StandardOutPath</key>
  <string>/Users/prh/Library/Logs/repair-plan.out.log</string>
  <key>StandardErrorPath</key>
  <string>/Users/prh/Library/Logs/repair-plan.err.log</string>
</dict>
</plist>
